1
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:06,940
(Shen Teng)

2
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:09,540
(Bai Jingting)

3
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,740
(Jia Bing)

4
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,820
(Hu Xianxu)

5
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:18,300
(Wang Anyu)

6
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,580
(Fan Chengcheng)

7
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,820
(Huang Jingyu)

8
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:24,860
(Wang Churan)

9
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:30,300
=Natural High S4 (Bonus Special)=

10
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,940
(Mounigou Scenic Area)

11
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:33,160
The game is called

12
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:34,240
Little Artist.

13
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:36,960
(Draw here)
Everyone works together to draw a scene.

14
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:37,840
Of our eight players,

15
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:38,920
(Rules)
six artists

16
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:40,240
get the exact scene.

17
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:41,200
The other two

18
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,840
only get a vague clue.

19
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,800
Each player has five seconds to draw.

20
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,280
Once everyone is done,

21
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:49,080
figure out which two got
the vague clues.

22
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:50,400
All right.

23
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,280
(Roles assigned)
Let's start with a practice round.

24
00:00:53,980 --> 00:01:02,660
(Exact scenario: A matador beauty pageant)

25
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:05,700
(Vague scenario: Bullfight)

26
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:07,340
(Thrilled)

27
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,820
(The undercover players
don't know each other)

28
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:09,640
(Exact scenario: A matador beauty pageant)

29
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:10,600
Who's first?

30
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:11,240
I'll go first.

31
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:12,160
(Vague scenario: Bullfight,
Undercover: Wang Churan, Hu Xianxu)

32
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:12,560
Okay.

33
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:14,460
(First artist up)

34
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,100
(Scene-setting music plays)

35
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:25,940
(Take turns drawing, moving left)

36
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:30,260
(What am I looking at?)

37
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:32,940
(Unidentified species)

38
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:34,080
Definitely an undercover.

39
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:35,840
That has to be one
of the undercover players.

40
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:44,840
That's right.

41
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,100
(Let me take a closer look)

42
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,360
What even is all this?

43
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,820
(Mystery creatures everywhere)

44
00:02:02,860 --> 00:02:03,860
(Teng, you get what I'm drawing, right?)

45
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:13,140
(What are these?)

46
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:13,340
(Not a single clue?)

47
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:13,540
(A pig? A bull?)

48
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:13,740
(A jellyfish? A bug?)

49
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:13,940
(Muscles? Huang Jingyu?)

50
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:14,100
(What am I supposed to do?)

51
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:15,060
(Who's actually undercover?)

52
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:16,700
(What do I do now?)

53
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:20,240
(Suspicion rising)
Hu's trying so hard to show what he knows.

54
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,820
(Acting like a detective)
I bet he barely knows anything.

55
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:25,540
(I've got this in the bag)

56
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:42,580
(Let me show you another move)

57
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,240
Bing, that move of yours is just...

58
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:46,780
(You have to admit, that's impressive)

59
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,580
(I give up)
There's no way I could pull that off.

60
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:55,440
The drawing is done.

61
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:56,920
(Round one ends)
Let's take a look.

62
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:57,980
(Bai Jingting, Lin Yi, Huang Jingyu,
Wang Churan, Jia Bing)

63
00:02:57,990 --> 00:02:59,180
(Fan Chengcheng, Lin Yi, Shen Teng,
Wang Churan, Hu Xianxu)

64
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:05,160
The full scene this round

65
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:07,680
was a matador beauty pageant.

66
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:10,680
What did Bing draw?

67
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:12,340
(Bing's masterpiece)

68
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:14,280
(Bai Jingting's drawing)
Wait, what's that on the far left?

69
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:15,640
A stick figure.

70
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:17,280
I was the first one up.

71
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,360
It's pretty obvious.

72
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:20,440
I started with a very clear drawing
of a bull.

73
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:21,960
(Teng is confused)
Is that a bull?

74
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:22,600
A bull.

75
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:23,760
Doesn't that look like a bull?

76
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:25,800
Then I added the details.

77
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,480
(Bull's eyes and nose)
The eyes, the nose,

78
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:28,840
(Bull's nose ring)
and its nose ring.

79
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:30,240
Looks like a pig.

80
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:31,080
I only had five seconds.

81
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:33,000
(Abstract art at its finest)
I think I captured it perfectly.

82
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,440
I think this...

83
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,360
(Praising his own work)
I think I did a great job.

84
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,040
(One well-fed bull)
That bull's been eating well.

85
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,640
Can't you tell a round face
from a long one?

86
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:41,760
No, listen.

87
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:44,080
How could I get that detailed
in five seconds?

88
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:45,720
But those numbers,

89
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:47,040
one, two, and three, seem suspicious.

90
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,760
Whoever wrote them better explain why.

91
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:49,580
(The artist behind 1, 2, 3)

92
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:50,840
Anyway,

93
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,080
there's no way I'm undercover.

94
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,000
All right, next.

95
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,520
He definitely drew a bull.

96
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,160
(Finally, someone gets it)
That's definitely not a pig.

97
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:56,640
Exactly.

98
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,560
It's obviously a bull.

99
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,240
Because it has

100
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,640
a nose ring, which pigs don't wear.

101
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:01,560
Louder. We can't hear you.

102
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:03,200
He drew a pig.

103
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:05,340
(Mr. Huang, you have changed)

104
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:10,240
Here's what I drew.

105
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,280
You drew me?

106
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,320
Yeah, Chengcheng competes

107
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:13,920
(Bodybuilding star)
at Mr. Olympia.

108
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,320
That's what I drew.

109
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,480
It represents the man

110
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:21,000
and the beauty pageant.

111
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:22,580
(Somewhat convinced)

112
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:25,000
Did you draw that part up there?

113
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,360
No, I only drew this much.

114
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,440
That turtle wasn't mine.

115
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,080
A turtle?

116
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:30,360
(The artist strongly disagrees)

117
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,320
A turtle?

118
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:32,320
That's a mouse.

119
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:33,160
A mouse?

120
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:33,780
See? The head is pointing down.

121
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:34,660
(What Churan thinks is the head)
Right there.

122
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:36,580
(I feel insulted, but I can't prove it)

123
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:37,980
(Guess what I am. No prizes)

124
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:38,840
An overhead light.

125
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:40,180
(Light)

126
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:43,100
(Is he on my team?)

127
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:44,660
(Completely baffled)

128
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,120
It's a beauty pageant.
Look at those muscles.

129
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,240
So I added an overhead light.

130
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:48,360
How else would you

131
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:49,440
show off those muscles

132
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,360
(Gym regulars know the trick)
without overhead lighting?

133
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:52,640
(Now I get it)

134
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,480
Who takes gym photos

135
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:56,040
without standing under the lights?

136
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:57,780
(Who came up with this guy?)

137
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,240
Overhead light!

138
00:04:59,240 --> 00:04:59,680
It's a beauty pageant.

139
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:01,160
They need contestant numbers.

140
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,120
One, two, three.

141
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:03,960
So you wrote those numbers?

142
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:05,760
Yeah, for the different contestants.

143
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:06,740
(Fair enough)

144
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:07,680
(Where are my teammates?)

145
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:10,000
I drew these two things.

146
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:11,780
(Dead serious)
Undercover.

147
00:05:13,850 --> 00:05:15,370
(Let the explaining begin)
Look at this.

148
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,000
Here's the thing.

149
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,720
There had to be a person, right?

150
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,560
(A man)
So I drew a man

151
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,000
here.

152
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,160
(Are you serious?)
A man?

153
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,560
(Say that again?)
A man?

154
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:25,500
(Brain, please start working)

155
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,880
That's his hair. Look.

156
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:28,420
(Hair)

157
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,520
And this is a bull.

158
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,560
That's supposed to be a bull?

159
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:34,360
(Trying very hard to understand)

160
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:34,640
Right.

161
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:35,600
But the brush

162
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:37,080
in my left hand

163
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:38,040
ran out of ink.

164
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:38,800
So that's as far as I got.

165
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,460
(Another artist isn't convinced)
I'm not buying that.

166
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,320
Now you're just making us
interpret your art.

167
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,080
Then why not draw an actual bull?

168
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:45,200
You call that a Shandong bull?

169
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:47,660
(Can't respond, can't explain)

170
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:48,120
No, wait.

171
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,720
What kind of bull is that?

172
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,000
Which part is which?

173
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,240
This is its head.

174
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,200
This is its body.

175
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,680
And that's its horn.

176
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:56,960
What's that weird thing

177
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,480
above the man?

178
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,040
I don't think I drew this.

179
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,400
(The mystery object's artist)
I added that.

180
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:04,680
I'm definitely not undercover.

181
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:07,260
(I tried my best)

182
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,400
Come on, explain

183
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:10,160
why you put that hat on the bull.

184
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:12,080
What is that thing supposed to be?

185
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,760
No, her drawing
doesn't look like a bull.

186
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,280
If you said it was...

187
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:18,600
a butchered piece of meat,

188
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,000
that'd be convincing.

189
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,200
And served on a plate, maybe.

190
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:23,180
(Nervous)

191
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:24,880
Wait, mine

192
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:26,380
(A bullfighter's trademark?)
is a cowboy hat.

193
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:26,920
A cowboy.

194
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,920
I drew this one.

195
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,160
I drew a medal.

196
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,360
What's that? A medal?

197
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,720
I thought it was a cowboy hat

198
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:38,600
seen from above.

199
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:39,960
It's a medal.

200
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:41,640
I wrote "hao" in the middle.
[*Good]

201
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:43,780
("Hao")
[*Good]

202
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:45,120
(In disbelief)
That says good?

203
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:46,320
The character for "hao"?

204
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:47,160
Yeah, "hao".

205
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:49,140
(Wait... are we on the same team?)

206
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,160
Who writes that on a medal?

207
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,280
I ran out of time.

208
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,640
What else could I have done

209
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:56,600
to make it look like a medal?

210
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,680
You could've written a one.

211
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:59,720
Or one, two, three.

212
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:01,640
What medal has that character
written on it?

213
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:02,640
I didn't have time
to think that far ahead.

214
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:03,960
Well, you didn't do a very good job.

215
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:05,820
(Something's not adding up)

216
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,480
I was second to last.

217
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,000
I saw the bull

218
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,080
and the pageant.

219
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:11,960
But it was missing a man.

220
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:13,240
So I drew the most recognizable

221
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:14,680
symbol for a man

222
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:15,760
you see in public.

223
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,040
A restroom sign?

224
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,680
Did you have to say it like that?

225
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:21,680
That's ridiculous.

226
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:24,760
(Adding insult to injury)
You had no idea what to draw,

227
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:25,880
so you just drew a person.

228
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:29,920
First of all,

229
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:32,480
these drawings...
I mean, these artists...

230
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,320
These artists right here...

231
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:35,680
I'm suspicious of all of them.

232
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:37,300
(Undercover in danger)

233
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:38,800
But Teng's drawing?

234
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:40,680
That one doesn't bother me.

235
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,120
Because at first,

236
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:43,520
I wanted to draw a cowboy hat too.

237
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:44,960
It's the obvious thing to draw.

238
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:46,580
(Great minds think alike)

239
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:47,920
As for Jingyu's drawing...

240
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:50,880
It's a beauty pageant,
not a pageant for you.

241
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:54,240
Showing off your muscles
doesn't prove a thing.

242
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:55,360
And why would anyone

243
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,640
win a medal at a beauty pageant?

244
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:57,920
So I'm suspicious of all of them.

245
00:07:58,360 --> 00:07:59,400
Who do I think is undercover?

246
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,280
It sure isn't me.

247
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,840
I was going to write an acrostic poem,

248
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:03,560
but I ran out of time.

249
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:04,880
(That's allowed?)

250
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:06,280
At least I got "beauty" in there.

251
00:08:06,730 --> 00:08:08,280
Bulls race beneath the stars.

252
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:09,710
Beauty blooms like a painting.

253
00:08:09,710 --> 00:08:11,380
(Bulls hints at matador,
beauty hints at the pageant)

254
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:16,320
(Always leave a paper trail)
I made sure I had proof.

255
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:17,880
Well,

256
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:19,000
out of all these artists,

257
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,400
we somehow got a calligrapher.

258
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:22,520
I'm most suspicious

259
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:23,880
of Lin Yi and his overhead lighting.

260
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:24,880
(Me?)

261
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,880
My one, two, three is solid.

262
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,000
I think the three of us

263
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,320
who went first

264
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:30,920
should be in the clear.

265
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,360
Think about it.
Before the music even played,

266
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:34,360
I drew a bull.

267
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:36,600
Lin Yi's one, two, three makes sense.

268
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,920
And then there's the muscular guy.

269
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:40,680
Bai's drawing looks suspicious.

270
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:43,660
(Teng's suspect No. 1)
Bai.

271
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:44,360
(Teng's suspect No. 2)
Hu.

272
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:45,880
Of course,

273
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:48,200
Churan is the most suspicious of all.

274
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:49,740
(Teng's suspect No. 3)

275
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:50,560
Why?

276
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:51,400
(One last attempt to save herself)

277
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,560
(I'm not even going to start)
What on earth did you draw?

278
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:54,440
(The two key clues: man and bull)
Look at the two key clues.

279
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:56,360
Your running stick figure and...

280
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,440
(Running stick figure)

281
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:58,760
(An unidentifiable blob)
That blob...

282
00:08:58,800 --> 00:08:59,720
Those are way off.

283
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:02,560
(Well, that didn't work)

284
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:04,520
(Throwing her teammate under the bus)
Churan, you keep saying

285
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:05,960
those are a bull and a man.

286
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:07,260
(Not listening)

287
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:08,360
You could draw a smiley face

288
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:10,080
(Still piling on)
and claim it's a woman.

289
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:11,760
(Bull + man = beef brisket)
That's beef brisket.

290
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,080
(The jokes keep coming)
Beef brisket.

291
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,160
Beef brisket?

292
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:17,520
Wrong.

293
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,840
The most important detail

294
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:20,520
is those three strands of hair.

295
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:23,440
Three... three strands of hair?

296
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,000
A guy with just three hairs?

297
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,720
If it were a woman,

298
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,920
I'd have drawn two braids.

299
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:29,760
Okay, I get it.

300
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:30,560
You got it?

301
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:32,280
(Trust +1)
That's how I'd draw a guy too.

302
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:34,560
I actually think Bai is pretty suspicious.

303
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:35,920
He's way too excited.

304
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:36,800
(Bai has had enough)

305
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:37,920
You could just copy the others

306
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,400
and draw a person.

307
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:40,720
Exactly.

308
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:41,920
I think you're...

309
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:42,760
A...

310
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:46,160
a restroom sign
for a matador beauty pageant?

311
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:46,920
I think...

312
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,920
(About to lose his mind)
I drew a man!

313
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,720
Someone already drew the muscles.

314
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:53,560
Why would you draw another man?

315
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:55,380
(That's a fair question)

316
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:56,780
(Out of the hot seat for now)

317
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:59,160
That overhead lighting is a stretch.

318
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:00,440
A real stretch.

319
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,000
It's obviously a light, Teng.

320
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,880
(Joining the pile-on)
It looks like someone drew an animal

321
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:05,640
and messed it up.

322
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,040
But as for Hu's drawing,

323
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:09,960
I'm not so sure about that either.

324
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:12,520
(Under suspicion again)
That doesn't look much like a medal,

325
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:13,640
if you ask me.

326
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:15,040
Looks more like a pie.

327
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:16,880
Sounds like you made that up afterward.

328
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:19,240
Go ahead, vote me out.

329
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:20,880
(Taking someone down with him)
But that light

330
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:22,680
and that men's restroom sign...

331
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:23,760
A man!

332
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:24,940
(Show my art some respect)

333
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,200
Men's restroom.

334
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,240
At least I drew a man,

335
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:30,040
which makes more sense than a light.

336
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:31,280
Seriously,

337
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:31,800
when I saw Lin Yi's drawing,

338
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:34,280
I thought it was a UFO.

339
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,400
I thought the undercover had gone crazy.

340
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:37,400
Isn't that a jellyfish?

341
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:38,160
No!

342
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:40,640
Even if I were undercover,
I wouldn't draw a UFO.

343
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:41,640
How would I even explain that?

344
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:42,640
Who knows what you were thinking?

345
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,080
You drew a light
and the numbers one, two, three.

346
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:45,600
How were we supposed to understand that?

347
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:46,600
Contestant numbers.

348
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,160
Even calling it a light is a stretch.

349
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:51,040
Anyway, I'm voting for beef brisket.

350
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:51,920
Beef brisket.

351
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,160
I'm telling you,
Wang Churan is definitely undercover.

352
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:56,080
It has to be Wang Churan.

353
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:56,640
It's obvious.

354
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:59,440
She and Bai both look like
they were copying

355
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,760
what the others had already drawn.

356
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:03,940
(Time to vote)
Three, two, one. Vote.

357
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:05,760
(Bai Jingting: 3, Lin Yi: 1, Wang Churan: 4)

358
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:07,700
(Eliminated this round: Wang Churan)
Churan, you're out.

359
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:08,360
All I can say

360
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:09,360
is that you've all got me wrong.

361
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,080
Well, in that case,

362
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:11,960
you seriously need drawing lessons

363
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:14,440
if you had the exact scenario.

364
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:16,440
I didn't vote for you.

365
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,800
I could tell yours was a bull.

366
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,080
Churan's clue was...

367
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:21,960
the vague scenario.

368
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:25,720
Really?

369
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,200
Well, Churan...

370
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,640
There was no way to save you.

371
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,640
That's all I can say.

372
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,160
(Oh no, I voted out my teammate)

373
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:34,040
Let's see the next set of clues.

374
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:37,260
(Exact scenario:
A relaxing childhood summer break)

375
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:39,640
(Vague scenario: Childhood)

376
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:41,320
(Next round begins)
Bing's up first.

377
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,240
He's drawing first.

378
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:47,110
(Exact scenario:
A relaxing childhood summer break)

379
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:52,380
(Vague scenario: Childhood,
Undercover: Wang Churan (out), Hu Xianxu)

380
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:54,140
(Almost went over time)

381
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,660
(What a masterpiece)

382
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:56,600
Nope.

383
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,280
This...

384
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:59,300
(Even the artist can't look)

385
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:08,720
Hu is undercover.

386
00:12:08,940 --> 00:12:10,660
(Something's not right)

387
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:25,700
(Round two ends)

388
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:26,880
I can't wait to see this.

389
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:28,260
(Jia Bing, Shen Teng,
Fan Chengcheng, Huang Jingyu)

390
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:29,220
(Hu Xianxu, Bai Jingting, Lin Yi)

391
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:32,120
The scene for this round

392
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:34,600
was a relaxing childhood summer break.

393
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:35,440
(Confident as always)

394
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:36,600
My masterpiece

395
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:38,040
is both expressive and realistic.

396
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,120
(Bing's art class is in session)
For this masterpiece,

397
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:43,200
I was inspired
by my childhood summer break.

398
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:45,440
So I made a book the centerpiece.

399
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:46,960
This is a book.

400
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:47,640
A what?

401
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:48,320
(Book)
A book.

402
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:48,880
(Uncle?)
A book?

403
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:50,440
Not your uncle.

404
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,480
A book. As in, reading.

405
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,280
(The model student)
An exam prep book.

406
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,600
You love studying that much?

407
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:56,200
Even reading on summer break?

408
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:57,280
But look.

409
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,280
What's the final touch?

410
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:01,400
(Who knows the answer?)

411
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:02,880
(What an imagination)
I think it's a kite.

412
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:03,960
(Everyone's paying attention)
Throw the book away.

413
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:04,720
Toss the book.

414
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:05,520
Throw it.

415
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:07,100
(A+ students)
Exactly. School's out.

416
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:09,720
(Here's the point)
Summer break is the theme,

417
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,760
and the book is just a prop.

418
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:11,600
That's the abstract part.

419
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,920
(Teacher, I get it)
That makes sense.

420
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,760
I drew this part in the corner.

421
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,240
First, here's the mouth.

422
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,160
(Mouth)

423
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:18,960
And the mustache.

424
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:19,540
(Mustache)

425
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,280
Put them together, and you've got Bing.

426
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:24,020
(Who's that supposed to be?)
What is that?

427
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:25,100
(That's supposed to be me?)

428
00:13:25,780 --> 00:13:28,220
(Scanning for similarities...
none found)

429
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,420
(Instant apology)
Sorry, Bing.

430
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:31,280
No, I'm not scared.

431
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:32,960
The clue said childhood.

432
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:35,720
It reminded me
of that kids' clothing game,

433
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,680
so I drew Bing.

434
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:39,400
(Defending Bing)
You had time to draw all that,

435
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:41,160
but not his eyes?

436
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:42,680
You could've at least given him eyes.

437
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:45,140
(Too scared to look.
Please be my imagination!)

438
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:47,360
I already spent plenty of time

439
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:48,400
(I tried)
on Bing.

440
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,120
It looks just like him.

441
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,320
He looks ready to jump out
of the drawing.

442
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:53,720
Why did you draw a sun?

443
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:54,440
What's the sun supposed to mean?

444
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,000
Summer break.

445
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:56,640
The sun represents summer break.

446
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:58,000
Doesn't the sun shine in winter too?

447
00:13:58,400 --> 00:13:58,880
Because it's hot.

448
00:13:59,320 --> 00:13:59,640
So...

449
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:04,000
Okay, I'm making this up as I go.

450
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,120
You could also see this

451
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,280
as...

452
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:08,280
(Only the artist could explain this)
a swing. Nice and relaxing.

453
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:08,840
This...

454
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:09,480
How can you possibly...

455
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:11,040
(Do you even believe that?)

456
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:13,320
You're trying to fool Bing, aren't you?

457
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:15,240
No, listen.

458
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,520
That part was an afterthought.

459
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:16,880
But this part?

460
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:18,200
I really did want to draw Bing.

461
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:20,080
(Back to the point)
He represents childhood.

462
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:20,680
Childhood?

463
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,480
Bing reminds you of childhood?

464
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,120
Kids' clothing.

465
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:25,120
From that game we played the other day.

466
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:27,240
You wore Bing-brand kids' clothes?

467
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:30,520
That's Bing right there?

468
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:31,120
Next.

469
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,760
Mine's really simple.

470
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:34,280
I only had five seconds,

471
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:35,640
so I drew something
that reminded me of childhood.

472
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:36,880
A giant lollipop.

473
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:38,600
(The toughest critic)
What's that got to do with summer break?

474
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,440
It's supposed to be relaxing.

475
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:40,320
Eating candy makes you happy.

476
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,480
And that's relaxing?

477
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:43,640
(I've got a question)
Why not popsicles for summer break?

478
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:44,880
If I'd drawn a popsicle,

479
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:45,880
it would've been a rectangle

480
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:46,680
with a stick on the end.

481
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:48,800
You'd definitely have voted me out.

482
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:50,160
A lollipop was safer.

483
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:51,640
You eat lollipops when it's that hot?

484
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:52,320
Even as a kid?

485
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:54,460
(No regrets)
Why do you care what I ate?

486
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,600
Why are you...

487
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:57,720
Why are you being so harsh?

488
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:58,640
Now you've got a problem with candy?

489
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:01,940
(Something's fishy)

490
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:05,560
He can't find it.

491
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:06,800
He can't find his own drawing.

492
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:09,160
Wait, let me look.

493
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:10,360
Is that supposed to be a person?

494
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,680
(Not even close)

495
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:13,560
I think Bai's just making stuff up.

496
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:16,200
Artist Bai.

497
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:18,280
You can tell what this is, right?

498
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:19,360
Your autograph.

499
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:20,000
Skiing.

500
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:21,320
(All wrong)

501
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,120
It's a kid flying a kite.

502
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,640
That was my childhood.

503
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:29,140
(That's my childhood too)

504
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:31,000
This one's mine.

505
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,120
This is...

506
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:32,960
two people.

507
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:33,560
(People)

508
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:36,200
He's crouching down like this.

509
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,760
And that's a manhole cover.

510
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:38,400
You see it, right?

511
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:38,840
A manhole cover.

512
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:41,740
(Are we supposed to?)

513
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:42,680
On top of a manhole cover?

514
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,840
Isn't that a crab?

515
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:45,520
A crab?

516
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:46,120
(Actually, he has a point)

517
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:47,600
No, these are two...

518
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,960
Two kids playing slap cards
by a manhole.

519
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,080
(Teng has questions)
Why play there?

520
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,280
Because the manhole cover helps.

521
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,360
The uneven surface

522
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:56,800
makes the cards easier to flip.

523
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,040
(Slap-card expert)
Didn't you play like that as kids?

524
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,160
We played on flat ground.

525
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:00,280
That's harder.

526
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:01,640
We played down in the manhole.

527
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:02,740
(Now that's a whole new level)

528
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:04,540
(What a stinky game)
Slap cards in the sewer?

529
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:06,400
Anyway, that's how I spent my childhood.

530
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:07,220
(Childhood Once More: The Slap-Card Years)

531
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:08,960
That definitely fits childhood.

532
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:13,340
(Still not letting it go)
And this is Bing?

533
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:15,460
(He's never living this down)

534
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:18,680
I was just about to ask

535
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:20,240
how you could even criticize
Lin Yi's drawing.

536
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,600
This is clearly a sun.

537
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:22,400
Originally,

538
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,720
I wanted to draw a sun too.

539
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,200
(Great minds think alike)
A sun with a smiley face.

540
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,080
That would've captured

541
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,880
a childhood summer break better.

542
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:28,800
But someone had already drawn a sun,

543
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,480
so I went with a bike instead.

544
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,360
I used to ride my bicycle all summer,

545
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,360
hanging out with my classmates.

546
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:36,720
(Here comes the challenge)
You had a bicycle back then?

547
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:37,880
My family had one bicycle

548
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,380
(The family bike)
for all seven of us.

549
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,720
Okay, that's fair.

550
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:43,340
(Convinced)

551
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:47,360
Now that looks like a crab.

552
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:49,160
(Still obsessed with crabs)

553
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:50,320
There's your real crab.

554
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:51,520
Leave Lin Yi alone.

555
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:53,760
There are two crabs in this picture.

556
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,800
(Crab No. 2, Crab No. 1)
Two giant crabs, side by side.

557
00:16:56,060 --> 00:16:58,500
(The crab artist is delighted)

558
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:00,840
This is a tree.

559
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,160
This is an island,

560
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:06,360
and here's a person.

561
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:08,160
I was picturing

562
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:08,920
a trip to Sanya.

563
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:10,160
(Going where?)

564
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,360
A summer trip to Sanya.

565
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:12,640
(Team Sanya vs. Team No Sanya)
Sanya for summer vacation?

566
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,080
Yeah.

567
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:14,400
For summer vacation?

568
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,160
Isn't that more of a winter destination?

569
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,800
It doesn't matter which island.

570
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:17,760
Just an island.

571
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:18,320
Any island.

572
00:17:19,120 --> 00:17:20,040
An island getaway.

573
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,720
(Something catches his eye)
Who drew that butterfly?

574
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:23,880
That's not a butterfly. It's a book.

575
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,600
Which butterfly? This one?

576
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:25,960
This one.

577
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:28,060
(The forgotten butterflies)

578
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:28,920
Who drew it?

579
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:29,400
Who drew that?

580
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:30,560
Not me.

581
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,680
(Mr. Huang has a suspect)
It was Hu.

582
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:33,760
Nobody's owning up to it.

583
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:34,360
Which one?

584
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,960
Did you draw this, Hu?

585
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:37,360
What butterfly?

586
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:38,040
This one. What's it supposed to be?

587
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:39,760
I was trying to show
how sweet the lollipop was,

588
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:41,000
but I ran out of time.

589
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:41,840
Very sweet?

590
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:42,200
Sweet?

591
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,960
I meant it was really sweet.

592
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:45,840
I think No. 2 and No. 3...

593
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:46,120
No, wait.

594
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:48,480
(Under suspicion)
I drew the sun first.

595
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:49,600
Because summer's hot.

596
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:52,600
Bing, kids' clothes, and childhood.

597
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:55,160
(You see my point?)

598
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:57,240
I really want to draw another round.

599
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:57,980
(Can't contain his artistic spirit)

600
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,680
I think it's the lollipop.

601
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,560
The lollipop...

602
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:05,160
(Exactly what I was thinking)
I think Hu cleverly

603
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,600
came up with all these ideas

604
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,080
from that song.

605
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:09,840
If you vote for me,

606
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:10,920
(Here comes the threat)
I'm voting out

607
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:11,560
that giant bicycle of yours.

608
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,400
Then I'm voting for him.

609
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,720
(Not scared one bit)
I'm voting for Hu.

610
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:14,840
That whole sweetness excuse?

611
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,440
You were obviously
drawing something else,

612
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:17,120
then you realized

613
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,640
your clue didn't match ours,

614
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:19,680
so you stopped explaining.

615
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:20,960
I didn't.

616
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,040
(Still denying it)
I swear I wasn't thinking that.

617
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:25,760
(Not buying it)
Then why didn't you explain the butterfly?

618
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:26,840
But this round,

619
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:28,080
(Objection)
Bing is the worst.

620
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,840
I mean the Bing that Bai drew.

621
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,140
(Attention shifts elsewhere)

622
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:32,560
And we're letting that slide?

623
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:32,960
No, hold on.

624
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:35,160
(Why am I getting dragged into this?)
Bing. Kids' clothes and childhood.

625
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,680
That's two clues right there.

626
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,850
(Lesson learned)
Next time, I'll draw

627
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:39,400
something simpler,

628
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:40,640
something everyone can recognize.

629
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:44,260
(Sorry)

630
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:45,660
(So sorry)

631
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:47,140
(I'll behave. Please stop)

632
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:48,320
You know, it does kind of look like him.

633
00:18:48,340 --> 00:18:50,080
(Chengcheng, are you serious?)

634
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:51,280
If you're saying that's me,

635
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:53,200
I guess I can live with it.

636
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:54,480
And Chengcheng's idea

637
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:56,560
(Throwing Chengcheng under the bus)
of a relaxing childhood summer break?

638
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:58,080
A trip to Sanya?

639
00:18:58,080 --> 00:18:59,160
Doesn't Shandong...

640
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,880
Doesn't Qingdao have beaches too?

641
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:03,320
Don't you go on trips
during summer break?

642
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,960
(Gen Z face-off)
To Sanya? In that heat?

643
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,240
It could be any island!

644
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:08,000
What, trying to see
how much heat you can stand?

645
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,960
Then why not just say
it's some island?

646
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,240
Actually, Sanya...

647
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:12,600
(Voice of reason)
Summer is actually

648
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:14,800
its second major...

649
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:15,400
Peak season?

650
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:15,960
Yeah, peak season.

651
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:17,240
Then we have to vote Bai out.

652
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:18,440
(Switching targets)
We don't have a choice.

653
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:18,720
No, wait.

654
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:20,360
(Still after Hu)
We can vote out the lollipop guy.

655
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:24,040
I think Chengcheng's suspicious too.

656
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:25,360
In the first round...

657
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:26,280
Remember round one?

658
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:29,280
The undercover clue
was a bull and a man,

659
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,160
and all he drew was a bull.

660
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:31,400
Chengcheng's a possibility.

661
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:33,320
(Secretly thrilled)
And this time he drew

662
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:33,760
an island.

663
00:19:35,420 --> 00:19:36,500
(Totally lost)
Are you talking about me?

664
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,800
But Chengcheng asked

665
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:42,960
to go first.

666
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,080
(Playing innocent)
If he were undercover...

667
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:45,080
That was why he did that.

668
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:45,640
Can I go first

669
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:46,600
next round?

670
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:47,360
(Desperate to get drawing)

671
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:48,520
So who should we vote out?

672
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:49,760
(Here's your chance)

673
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:50,620
Anyone but me.

674
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:51,200
(Anyone else will do)

675
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:51,920
I just...

676
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:52,560
Pick someone.

677
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:53,360
I just want to draw...

678
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:54,440
(Art comes first)
I think...

679
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:56,040
I think it's the slap-card drawing.

680
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:57,800
I couldn't even tell
those were slap cards.

681
00:19:58,440 --> 00:20:00,970
(Why me?)
I nailed the first round.

682
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,120
I got it exactly right.

683
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:04,360
(That enormous overhead light)
You mean that giant light you drew?

684
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:04,920
Really?

685
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,960
I even put one, two, three on it.

686
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:09,480
Stop picking apart people's drawings!

687
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:11,080
Focus on their reasoning!

688
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,520
But that's exactly my point.

689
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:14,360
(Let me explain)
As soon as the clue was revealed,

690
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:15,480
he started making excuses

691
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,560
and claiming he'd drawn slap cards.

692
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:19,680
Three, two, one.

693
00:20:19,680 --> 00:20:20,440
Please vote now.

694
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:21,020
(Hu Xianxu: 3, Lin Yi: 2, Bai Jingting: 2)

695
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,160
(Eliminated this round: Hu Xianxu)

696
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:22,680
Hu.

697
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:23,780
(You've got to be kidding)
Me?

698
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:24,880
I got voted out after all that?

699
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:26,080
Yep. Three votes.

700
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:27,560
I don't think Hu's undercover.

701
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,200
He was third to draw,

702
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:30,000
and he drew a lollipop.

703
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,680
(I trusted you, Hu)
The childhood clue seemed pretty...

704
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:33,560
Hu was...

705
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:39,200
Undercover.

706
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,400
He was given the vague scenario.

707
00:20:42,060 --> 00:20:44,460
(It was you the whole time?)

708
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:46,280
(You drew that right next to mine)
Hu, you drew this?

709
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:47,400
(All that trust...)
I don't think Hu's undercover.

710
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:48,200
Bai.

711
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:49,020
(All those good times...)

712
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:50,300
(Was it all a lie?)

713
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:53,160
How did you know?

714
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,480
(Neither can believe it)
What's wrong with drawing a lollipop?

715
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,520
We both knew it was Hu

716
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,320
(We saw right through him)
as soon as he got

717
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:58,800
his clue card.

718
00:20:58,800 --> 00:20:59,960
Right after the first drawing round,

719
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:02,220
(Called it)
we'd already figured it out.

720
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:03,960
Please vote now.

721
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:07,020
(Vote result: Bai Jingting)

722
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:09,760
I thought I was in the clear.

723
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:11,040
I even thought

724
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:13,200
(The fox shows his true colors)
they'd never catch me.

725
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:15,360
But what really bothers me

726
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:16,920
is that I thought Churan was innocent.

727
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:18,600
(Giggles)
I never thought she was undercover.

728
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:20,560
How could she draw something like that?

729
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:22,280
It was such a dead giveaway.

730
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:23,760
I actually thought she might be innocent.

731
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:26,540
(Look who's talking)
Your first drawing was terrible too.

732
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,480
Who puts "good" on a medal?

733
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:33,800
At least I drew the right thing.

734
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:36,500
(Wang Churan's drawing)

735
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:37,600
You sure you did?

736
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:41,440
In that last round,

737
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,440
the good guys won.

738
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:43,960
They caught the undercover players
in both rounds.

739
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:44,920
Impressive.

740
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:45,920
Really impressive.
